WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:05.760
Daisy felt flustered. She wasn't sure what to say to everyone.

2
00:00:05.761 --> 00:00:10.375
Parker had said she talked to the crickets and set them free.

3
00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.354
But most kids probably wouldn’t believe it.

4
00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:18.179
But what if some did? That would cause lots of trouble.

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.380
Suddenly Kaleem jumped to his feet.

6
00:00:21.381 --> 00:00:25.892
"It wasn't Daisy! But Parker's right about something.

7
00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:30.586
I was involved. I'm the one who set the crickets free!"

8
00:00:30.587 --> 00:00:33.899
Everyone gasped, including Daisy.

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.056
" You did it?" she

10
00:00:37.057 --> 00:00:40.471
cried. "Yes." Kaleem looked

11
00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:43.327
sheepish. "I felt bad they were trapped, like you

12
00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:48.126
said. So I pretended to look for something in my desk while everyone left for

13
00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:50.602
recess. Then I tipped over the

14
00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:56.391
tank." Mr. Neal frowned. "I wish you'd talked to me instead of doing that,

15
00:00:56.392 --> 00:01:01.112
Kaleem." "I'm sorry." Kaleem didn't sound very sorry to Daisy.

16
00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:03.695
"But Daisy said crickets are nocturnal, right?

17
00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.499
That means they don't like being out in the daytime."

18
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.183
"Dude, we all know what nocturnal means," Parker said.

19
00:01:11.184 --> 00:01:16.191
Kaleem ignored him. "That's probably why they all disappeared.

20
00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:20.427
They all scurried outside to get away from the bright lights inside."

21
00:01:20.428 --> 00:01:23.601
"That makes sense," Mr. Neal said.

22
00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:27.731
Most of the kids nodded. Daisy was relieved.

23
00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:31.319
But she still couldn't believe Kaleem had released the crickets.

24
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.551
"I know you meant well, Kaleem," Mr. Neal said.

25
00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:38.614
"But you broke some rules, which affected our whole class.

26
00:01:38.615 --> 00:01:40.879
I'd like you to stay after school today.

27
00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.589
We'll have a conversation about how you could have handled this situation differently."

28
00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:50.704
"Okay," Kaleem said. He shot Daisy a smile.

29
00:01:50.705 --> 00:01:54.819
She smiled back, relieved that he wasn't in too much trouble.

30
00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.085
But then she noticed Parker scowling at her.

31
00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:03.429
She wondered if he still thought she had something to do with freeing the crickets.

32
00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.185
She didn't really care about what Parker thought.

33
00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:12.295
She did care about Grace's thoughts, though, and Grace was giving her a curious look.

34
00:02:12.296 --> 00:02:16.837
Daisy gulped. Was it possible that Grace knew the truth?

35
00:02:16.838 --> 00:02:19.932
Her eyes flicked to Beatrice again.

36
00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:26.782
"I'll have to be much more careful from now on," Daisy thought.

37
00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:29.871
"Otherwise I might get Beatrice in trouble.

38
00:02:29.872 --> 00:02:37.112
Even worse, I might lose my ability to talk to animals!"

39
00:02:37.113 --> 00:02:41.734
*** On the way home, Daisy explained everything to

40
00:02:41.735 --> 00:02:46.549
Beatrice. "Oh, that's why Kaleem isn't with you today," Beatrice

41
00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:49.486
said. "I'm glad you spoke up for the crickets.

42
00:02:49.487 --> 00:02:55.914
You're already doing what you're supposed to be, uh . . ." She stopped talking.

43
00:02:55.915 --> 00:02:59.557
"Wait, what do you mean?" Daisy asked.

44
00:02:59.558 --> 00:03:01.696
"What am I supposed to be doing?

45
00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:05.945
Does this have something to do with my ability to talk to animals?"

46
00:03:05.946 --> 00:03:11.939
"Oh, it's nothing like that!" Beatrice laughed loudly.

47
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.908
"I just mean you're good at talking to all kinds of animals.

48
00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:19.941
Hey, don't you have to walk Scamp?"

49
00:03:19.942 --> 00:03:26.521
Daisy realized Beatrice was right about Scamp. She had to go over to Mrs. Ortiz's house.

50
00:03:26.522 --> 00:03:32.774
"But that doesn't mean I'm going to give up asking her questions," Daisy thought.

51
00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:36.254
She still wanted to know how this had happened.

52
00:03:36.255 --> 00:03:43.914
After all, it wasn't every day that an ordinary girl turned into Daisy Dolittle!

